# Cross-doc consistency

The documents below live in the internal (non-public) documentation set — see
docs-ssot-and-structure. When changing any of:
- the system spec
- the architecture overview (or its diagrams)
- the implementation plan
- the e2e testing strategy
- the project status

check consistency (no contradiction) at least on:
- registry state vs runtime watch activation
- DSC conditions (`Accepted`, `AccessGranted`, derived `Ready`) and watch activation formula
- optional unified CRD / bootstrap (S1–S2) vs future DSC-driven registry
- manifest / MCR track vs unified snapshot registry (separate concerns)
- stage / progress in the project status vs tables in the implementation plan and test IDs in the e2e testing strategy

The related long-form ADR must not disagree with the internal system spec without an explicit documented transition.

Fix inconsistencies in the same change or document a temporary divergence and follow-up.
